[00:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] &gt;&gt; As you no doubt have heard, the H3 model'

[00:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from Hailuo is an extremely capable model and a serious competitor to at least C Dance 2.0. C Dance 2.5, that\'s a whole other animal, haven\'t played with it yet. But, I have spent the past 48'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hours immersed in H3 to see what this sucker could do. Like C Dance, H3 is a multimodal model, which means you can throw image references, audio references, video references at it, mix them all up, and do all the kinds of video editing that you\'re used to with'

[00:53] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: A split screen shows four animated characters, resembling developers or researchers, working on laptops in a modern office setting.
AUDIO: 'the C Dance model as well. It is exceptionally good at fine-grain editing, and that is surgical edits within the prompt that we\'re hearing so much about with other models. Now, I\'m a few days late to this party in terms of sharing a video, and there\'s a reason for that. This model is so capable that'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if you\'re going to show great examples of it, if you\'re going to find out what it\'s capable of, you\'d better learn how to prompt it properly. And trying to rush out a video the day the model came out just wasn\'t going to serve that purpose. And because the necessity for well-structured prompts is becoming more'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and more important, you see creators all over the place showing you how they\'re using LLMs to create these prompts. Instead, I decided to vibe code my own H3 prompt generator that I could reuse, save the prompts, and tweak, and have'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'presets. I\'m going to show you briefly how it works, but it is running a server locally on my machine. It\'s touching Ollama, and recording and editing video just doesn\'t mix with it very well. But, I want to show you its basic capabilities so you understand how I got the prompts for the videos that I\'m'

[01:44] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The creator demonstrates the H3 prompt builder UI, showing input fields for "What should happen?", "Choose the look" (visual style, camera feel, shot flow), and a "Ready to copy" section for the generated prompt.
AUDIO: 'going to show you, because I\'m super pleased with the output that I\'ve gotten from these. The general idea is that you put a basic idea of what your prompt is in this section here. What should happen? A female action superhero is fighting a series of mechanical spiders'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in a downtown city. The spiders and the superhero are scaling the walls with incredible agility, but in the end, the superhero wins. That\'s the arc. I choose a visual style. We have all kinds to choose from here. In this case, I chose'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'anime. We can also choose what the camera feels like. Is it cinematic? Is it pushing in? Is it handheld? Are we orbiting around the subject? I got examples of all of these. And then, how do the shots flow throughout the scene? Is it one continuous movement? Are we'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'doing multiple cinematic shots? Are we building some suspense? Based on what we choose from all of these, the prompt is going to be built. When you click to optimize that prompt, it\'s going to give you a detailed prompt optimized for H3, broken down into shots with specific'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'time and descriptions of everything, including all the camera movement and styles that you have defined here. So, I did all my testing over in OpenArt, and here is the video that we created with that prompt. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[02:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; I think that\'s pretty darn good. Lots of cuts, lots of action, looked great. But my little generator here allows us to'

[03:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'save the history of our prompts. And so, here is a version of that same prompt that instead of using anime, I chose visceral cinematic horror and chose for the shot flow horror escalation and reveal. That generated a completely'

[03:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different prompt, and here\'s how that one turned out. I won\'t be going back and forth between'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the generator and the finished video the whole time. I just wanted to show you where I was getting these prompts and basically how this worked. That generator I\'m going to make available at some point, but there\'s still some bugs in there that I want to work out. But just as an aside, I vibe coded this with natural language using ChatGPT. You can'

[03:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do the exact same thing. But if you want to know more about how I vibe coded this, let me know in the comments and we\'ll probably do a whole vibe coding series pretty soon. We\'ll start with an example that I actually didn\'t use my prompt generator for because the prompt'

[03:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'was so simple. And this is testing basic motion transfer. So, here\'s the original video. And the instruction is, transfer the'

[04:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'motion of the character in this video to the character in image one. And this is image one. That\'s all I had. And put her in a muddy cave tunnel. And here\'s what we got. Here\'s another example of using the same'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'basic prompt, but giving H3 two different styles to work with. The premise, of course, is silly. A clown is pushing a whale out of a helicopter, which falls to the ground and explodes into a pile of candy. And on the way down to the ground, the whale is'

[04:37] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: The creator discusses a generated video of a whale being thrown from a helicopter, highlighting AI inconsistencies.
AUDIO: 'thinking about what a great life it had as a Walmart greeter. This first example was done with more of a horror tone. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[04:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Now, I don\'t want to ignore the fact that he actually is throwing the whale up into the air instead of toward the ground. It corrects itself, but this is'

[05:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just one of those AI inconsistencies that happen. I\'m sure if I had run it again, it might have done better. But, one of the things I learned in this example is that if you don\'t tell it to create dialogue, it\'s not going to assume you want it. You don\'t have to write it out word for word, but you do'

[05:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'need to tell it in your basic prompt that you want the characters to talk. Then, when the prompt generates in the generator, it will give some dialogue. This example is basically the same prompt, but I gave it a more whimsical tone and told it to come up with dialogue.'

[05:27] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video shows a couple in a club-like setting, illustrating an attempt at character transformation.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; YOU\'RE GOING TO BE MY NEW STAR! [screaming] I USED TO BE A GREETER. I loved that job. You\'d never believe how much I loved it. The sea, it was my home. And now, I\'m free to be sweet.'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Now, like a lot of AI models, some of these results can be hit or miss. In some ways, this prompt succeeded greatly. The idea is that a couple is coming home, kind of, you know, a little inebriated from a fun day. They get approached by a gang of guys who want to'

[05:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rob them, and then they\'re supposed to turn into mechs and fight them. Here\'s what I actually got. &gt;&gt; Hand over the cash now.'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; So, they took care of the bad guys, but they didn\'t actually transform into mechs in that one chance I gave it to'

[06:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work. But, just about everything else in that video was amazing. The cinematography, the shot choices, the lighting, the dialogue, it all worked. This next example was simply a cat is chasing a mouse through a department store causing all kinds of chaos with'

[06:30] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video depicts a cat chasing a mouse through a department store in a 3D animation style.
AUDIO: 'silly music in the background. I gave it a 3D animation visual style, told it for the most part to be a smooth tracking shot. You\'ll notice in this particular prompt, it defined for every shot what the camera is doing, what the subject\'s doing, the environment, the lighting,'

[06:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and everything, and even the sound for every shot. And here\'s what we get. &gt;&gt; Meow. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[06:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Didn\'t look good for either of those animals at the end there. So far, there has been no style that I have thrown at this thing that it has not been able to'

[07:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do. Like this one here, which it calls gothic whimsy. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Peace.'

[07:19] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: The creator shows a video of himself, then demonstrates H3's precise editing by changing his shirt color and background to an ice cream museum.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Now, I want to show you a couple of examples of that precise editing that I was talking about. You can identify a section of the video that you want to edit leaving the rest of it completely'

[07:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'alone. Let\'s start with a basic video that we want to change. Here\'s the original video. All right, so I\'m going to sit here in this room and talk for, I don\'t know, I don\'t need to do 10 seconds or 15 seconds but maybe 20 15 10 All right, I\'ll do 10. I'

[07:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dropped in that video as the reference and said from 4 to 7 seconds his shirt turns red and for the entire video the background is an ice cream museum. All right, so I\'m going to sit here in this'

[07:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'room and talk for I don\'t need to do 10 seconds or 15 seconds but maybe 20 15 10 All right, I\'ll do 10. Absolutely nailed it. Changed the color of the shirt and the whole time he\'s in an ice cream museum. Now this video was created with'

[08:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this prompt here. An old woman is awakened by a sound in the middle of the night. She gets out of bed, puts on a robe and starts walking down the hall. As she approaches the bathroom door, she sees a light coming on from underneath and hears running water. She knocks'

[08:22] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated horror video of an old woman encountering a monster in a hallway is played, followed by an attempt to edit the monster and the woman's reaction.
AUDIO: 'gently on the door and says, "Sweetie, is that you?" The door opens rapidly and a terrifying monster with bulging eyes and bangs and slimy skin, I think that was supposed to say fangs, roars at her and she runs down the hall.'

[08:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Sweetie, is that you? &gt;&gt; Okay, now the biggest problem with that'

[08:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is she ran right past the monster. I mean there is a hall down there but my vision was that she was going to turn around and run back towards the camera. So I used the editing capabilities of the model to try two edits at a time and I probably should have only done one but'

[09:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here\'s what I did. So I brought in that video that we just watched as a reference video and this image of a character. I said replace the monster at the 8 second mark in the bathroom with the man in the image and instead of running down the hall at the end she'

[09:16] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video of a fantasy landscape with a rainbow and castle is shown, demonstrating an edited opening sequence.
AUDIO: 'runs toward and then past the camera lens. Here\'s what we ended up with. &gt;&gt; Sweetie, is that you? &gt;&gt; So it was kind of close. We didn\'t get'

[09:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the transformation of the monster doll, which I was bummed about. She ran down the hall and then she said, "Oh, wait, that\'s probably not a good idea. I think I\'ll run this way past the camera." Part of the opening sequence of this video was this clip here. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[09:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; So, it didn\'t have any sort of H3 on it and I wanted to use this as part of the opening. So, I used the edit feature. In this case, I dragged the video we just watched in as a reference image and then'

[10:11] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video with a man in a kitchen, showcasing a body horror transformation.
AUDIO: 'I said, "In the last 5 seconds of this video, have a giant, highly stylized H3 emerge from the clouds in the sky and make its way towards the front of the screen acting as a logo for the HiLo H3 model." And I only made the clip 5'

[10:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seconds. So, I didn\'t regenerate the entire clip again just to get that change at the last 5 seconds and here\'s what it gave us. So, I was literally able just to place'

[10:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that at the end of the original clip and I had exactly what I was going for. I want to show you this example because there was a happy accident involved, although it doesn\'t look too happy yet. This clip tells the story of a man who over the course of time is becoming'

[10:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'deformed somehow and shapeshifting into something horrible looking. Here\'s the clip that was generated. &gt;&gt; [panting and sighs] [groaning]'

[11:10] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video shows a man serving breakfast in a fantasy landscape, demonstrating a "happy accident" where a previous prompt influenced the output.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Right? So, in my mind, that experiment was over. That was pretty cool. I know that H3 is a relatively censored model, so I wasn\'t going to get any real blood and gore, but that was pretty cool effect. After I did that example, I'

[11:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'started working on the example I just showed you with the opening with the dragon. But, when I originally tested bringing this still image to life, what I didn\'t know was that the prompt about the man changing was still in the form, and so I ended up getting this.'

[11:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here we start with two cartoon sloths'

[11:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'agree to race each other by rolling down a grassy hill covered with daisies and sunflowers as other animals run alongside them. At the bottom of the hill, they both roll into a mud puddle, look at each other, and laugh. I ran that through 3D animation, dynamic'

[12:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The creator returns to the H3 prompt builder UI, showing options for "handheld realism" and "fast commercial style cuts" for an influencer video.
AUDIO: 'action sequence, and here\'s our result. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[12:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; H3 is also really good at creating influencer type videos. We\'ll start with a simple one. A beautiful TikTok influencer is giving us a quick cut tour of ice cream shops in Las Vegas. She is very chatty and likes to talk about what'

[12:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'she\'s tasting, and she giggles a lot. I used handheld realism as the camera feel and fast commercial style cuts for the shot, and here\'s what it gave us. &gt;&gt; Hey guys, let\'s go. First stop, the original scoop. So creamy, so sweet. I\'m going to be a'

[12:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'regular here. This place has the best vanilla I\'ve ever had. I\'m going to take a selfie with this. Thanks for watching. I\'ll see you next time. &gt;&gt; This prompt is simply a TikTok influencer is taking on a shopping trip where she\'s trying to pick out a pink'

[12:59] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video of a TikTok influencer shopping is shown, highlighting the need for explicit dialogue prompts.
AUDIO: 'skirt. Again, I forgot to say to add any dialogue or talking to the camera, and here\'s what we got. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; I know there\'s some weird AI head'

[13:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spinning there, but overall, this is pretty good, especially given that action. Still, my vision for this was that the influencer was going to talk to the camera. I went back to the prompt generator, told it to add some dialogue, and now we\'ve got this. &gt;&gt; Oh my gosh, I love this one.'

[13:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This one\'s cute, but maybe it\'s just a little too much. What do you guys think? Should I wear it? I\'m feeling so confident today. I think I found it. Thanks for watching, guys.'

[13:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; So, I thought that was pretty good, but this was a totally text-generated influencer, so I wanted to try it with a reference image. So, I used this character sheet and the exact same prompt, only this time I referenced the'

[13:57] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The creator is back on the H3 prompt builder UI, discussing adding dialogue to the influencer prompt.
AUDIO: 'photo of the influencer at the very top. &gt;&gt; Oh my gosh, I love this one. This one\'s cute, but maybe it\'s just a little too much. What do you guys think? Should I wear it? I\'m feeling so confident today. I think I found it.'

[14:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Thanks for watching, guys. &gt;&gt; So, it was during this next example that I got a whole new idea for the app itself. For the most part, I\'ve been using this as a text-to-video generator almost exclusively. I\'ve used some reference images, but I haven\'t done'

[14:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'anything with a start frame. Well, I thought if the prompt generator knows the context of the entire story here, what if it could generate an appropriate prompt to create a great starting image appropriate for exactly what it\'s saying it\'s going to do? But, what if we also'

[14:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had the option of creating a reference image? That is, a series of panels with the various graphical elements from the video that then the model could put together. Let me show you exactly what I\'m talking about. So, in this example, the idea was that it was the point of'

[14:49] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video shows a close-up of a caterpillar, demonstrating the "cocoon" concept with a cinematic look.
AUDIO: 'view of a caterpillar doing the whole cocoon thing and then maybe having second thoughts. So, I wanted a really good starting image for that. So, that\'s when I created this create an image prompt option. When you click that, you have the option of creating a starting image, like I said, that\'s going to be'

[15:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the first frame of your animation, or a reference image. I even have an option that rewrites the original video prompt if you use reference images to call out those specific elements. So, for this video, the prompt that was generated by'

[15:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the prompt generator for the image gave us this image here, which I thought was nice and creepy and visceral that I absolutely wanted to use it. So, I used that with the prompt that was generated and we got this. &gt;&gt; Cocoon. What is this? Wait, what am I doing?'

[15:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This can\'t be [music] right. No. No, I don\'t want to Hey, I\'m not feeling so good. &gt;&gt; I mean, I love the cinematic look of that, but I also wanted to see this idea'

[15:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in a more light and cartoony style. So, all I did in that prompt generator was change it to an animated style, regenerate the prompt, and now I have this. &gt;&gt; Cocoon. What is this? Wait, what am I doing?'

[15:53] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A generated video shows a man in a suit with a hang glider on a cliff, illustrating the use of a starting image.
AUDIO: 'This can\'t be right. No. No, I don\'t want to Hey, I\'m not feeling so good. &gt;&gt; Here\'s another example. This time I created both the starting image and a'

[16:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reference image and and created example videos from both techniques. The idea is Harry quits his job as an accountant to follow his dream of becoming a professional hang glider. That\'s all I wrote. It gave us this nice prompt here, and then I told it to generate a'

[16:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'suitable image prompt, and it did, and this is the image it gave us for the starting image. So, using the starting image technique, we got this. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; I\'m sorry, that is super impressive.'

[16:41] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The creator is back on the H3 prompt builder UI, showing the "mixed live action and hand-drawn animation" visual style.
AUDIO: 'When I had it generate a reference image version, it gave us this. So, we\'ve got him standing on the cliff, we\'ve got a close-up of the cliff by himself and his scattered supplies on the ground. So, to prompt this, I chose text with reference, I dragged in this image, and'

[16:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at the very bottom of the prompt here, there\'s a note that basically tells the model how to use the reference image. And here\'s what it gave us. &gt;&gt; [screaming]'

[17:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; While I was doing all this, under the visual style, I saw this one mixed live action and hand-drawn animation. And honestly, I sort of avoided it because I thought, well, I don\'t know if it\'s'

[17:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to be able to do that. But I thought, well, let\'s just give it a shot. So, I said, "A woman walking along a marina is greeted by a talking sea lion who invites her to live under the sea with him." And she accepts and they dive into the water together. I choose that mixed live and animated visual'

[17:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'style, and it gave us this. &gt;&gt; Join me, and I\'ll show you wonders beneath the surface. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[17:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Now, one of the other exciting things about this model is that they have made it available as open weight, which means that in theory, you could run this model on a local machine using ComfyUI or something else. However, they have a lot of restrictions around its use. If you'

[18:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are in the excluded territories, the US included, you are not licensed to use them at all. However, anyone can use the model as long as they go through a service that uses their API, like OpenArt or any other provider that gives'

[18:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you access to that. That way, they can use all their safety rails. don\'t have that ability. And in our country and others, they\'re just not going to let that fly. Let me know what you thought of the A3 model in the comments below. And if these are the types of things'

[18:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'re interested in keeping up with, well, why not subscribe to this channel if you haven\'t already, cuz we love looking at this stuff all the time. &gt;&gt; [music]'
